 | `POST /admin/backup` | Writes a compressed copy of the data directory to `{"dest"}` |
 
 Invoices: usage is costed per request at list price, summed per model, converted to cents, then the key's discount is applied.
+
+## Rate limiting
+
+`createServer({ rateLimit: { limit, windowMs } })`. Defaults: `{ limit: 60, windowMs: 60000 }`; fields you leave out fall back to the defaults. `limit` must be an integer and `windowMs` a number, both from 1 to `Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER`, otherwise `createServer` throws a `RangeError`. Time comes from the `now` option.
+
+- Every request except `GET /health` is limited, including requests that end in 401, 403 or 404. Limiting runs before auth and routing.
+- The key is the `x-api-key` header. Requests without one share the key `anonymous`.
+- Windows are fixed per key. A window starts at the key's first request and lasts `windowMs`. The next request at or after the window's end starts a new window.
+- Within a window the first `limit` requests are allowed. Later requests get `429` with the body `{"error":"rate_limited","retryAfter":N}` and a `Retry-After` header: whole seconds until the window ends, rounded up, at least 1.
+- Every limited response carries `X-RateLimit-Limit` and `X-RateLimit-Remaining` (requests left in the window after this one, never below 0).
+- `GET /health` is exempt: never rejected, never counted, no rate-limit headers.
+- Once 10,000 keys are tracked, windows that have ended are dropped, at most once per `windowMs`. This bounds memory and does not change any response.
